Initial commit: generic UGREEN NAS MCP server

SSH-based MCP server for UGREEN NAS (UGOS) covering daily ops: system
status/info/storage-pools, Docker (containers/images/networks/compose),
files (list/usage/mkdir/copy/move/remove/SFTP upload/download/rsync sync),
backups (create/list/verify/restore/schedule), and host networks.

- No hard-coded target facts; single-NAS config from ~/.ugnas-mcp/config.json
  with UGNAS_* env overrides and SSH-key auth.
- Every mutating tool returns a dry-run plan gated by a single-use,
  action-bound confirmation token; the exact planned commands are executed.
- All user input is POSIX shell-quoted before reaching the remote command.
- 37 tools; stdio by default with optional Streamable-HTTP (UGNAS_HTTP_PORT).
- 28 tests against a FakeExecutor (no real NAS required).
